{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>The rivers lifted</b> — After he mentioned earth and heavens, he mentioned seas and rivers, for they flow constantly. This is it: \"the rivers lifted their voice.\"" "<b>dakim</b> — they are the breakers, and the meaning is the same. For after they are dakim [crushed/breakers], they are lifted by the will of the Creator, when He sends His angels, which are the winds."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 93, :notes {1 "Bracketed gloss added to clarify the force of dakim in context; the root דכה conveys both 'crushed' and 'breaking waves.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:09.592249620Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}